title: '<localleader>v? : :SkgDescribeAtPoint'
pid: 48920e2c-3c65-4062-ba56-765d73c4fa3c
body: |2-
  As C-c v ? does in Emacs: says in plain sentences what the headline
  at point is, when it is a folder, then what each herald it shows
  means, the most informative first, with its own numbers and letters
  read out. Two screen lines or fewer show as a message, more in a
  scratch window below, which q closes. It changes nothing.
